  "narrative": "Validation closes the two remaining plausible positive lines. For H196, discovery suggested a very large feature_032 effect on outcome_014 within the feature_034=1 subgroup, but independent validation was essentially null and imprecise, with an estimate near zero and an interval spanning both meaningful and opposite effects; this does not support a clinically meaningful outcome_014 association and confirms a false-positive/non-replicating discovery pattern. For H19, the feature_042 versus feature_042 main effect on outcome_001 had a discovery estimate near the 10%-of-mean benchmark (about 0.044 versus benchmark about 0.0415) but its lower confidence bound was far below benchmark. The independent validation was signed negative, about -0.0096, with a wide interval that does not raise support above the benchmark and contradicts the discovery direction. Precision weighting these two similarly sized contrasts still leaves a combined point estimate below the outcome_001 clinical benchmark. I therefore reject H19 as a supported clinically meaningful association and close the feature_042-outcome_001 line, including the post-hoc positive subgroups H183, H189, and H192; their positive estimates are not interval-level clinically supported and were selected after seeing the main-effect signal. The supported set remains empty. Negative or non-replicating findings are now substantial: feature_054 is broadly null across the tested outcome panel; feature_002, feature_034, feature_060, and most feature_042 contrasts are null or clinically unsupported; feature_063 is mostly null except for an unresolved outcome_014 signal; feature_045 and several noisy outcome associations remain weak; and validated failures across H23, H26, H49, H57, H59, H87, H106, H196, and now H19 illustrate the high false-positive risk from high-variance outcomes and subgroup selection. The most informative remaining uncertainty is feature_063 level_002 versus level_001 for outcome_014: H114 has a discovery estimate about 0.036 with a zero-excluding interval but lower bound below the outcome_014 benchmark of about 0.0093. I reopen H114 as active and focus next analyses on whether feature_063 effects are coherent across outcomes (outcome_013, outcome_001, outcome_014 level_003, outcome_011), while also testing feature_045 on outcome_008 and outcome_011 and one feature_055 contrast, plus two broad 4-level categorical explorers. Acceptance for feature_063 will require a clinically interval-supported effect, preferably coherent main or subgroup effects or independent validation with a lower bound above the outcome-specific 10% benchmark; otherwise it will be closed. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 13 synthesis. Accepted claim set: empty. Closed major lines after validation/failure: feature_042-outcome_001 (H19 validation R164 negative wide; combined precision-weighted point below benchmark about 0.0415; H183/H189/H192 rejected as post-hoc unsupported), feature_032-outcome_014 subgroup line (H196 validation near null), feature_054 panel, feature_008 main panel, feature_060/feature_034/feature_002 broad weak/null panels, low-priority rare binary active claims closed. Deferred: H4 and H104 feature_045 main effect evidence but no strong case for active testing. Active next priorities: H114 (outcome_014 feature_063 level_002 vs level_001, positive zero-excluding discovery but lower below benchmark about 0.0093), H68/H69 (feature_045 on outcome_008/011), H99 (feature_055 level_001 vs level_003 outcome_014), H133/H134/H141 (feature_063 outcome_013, outcome_001, outcome_014 level_003), and proposed feature_063 outcome_011 plus feature_028/feature_036 broad categorical tests on outcome_014/outcome_001. Decision rule for feature_063: accept only if clinical interval lower bound at or above outcome-specific 10%-of-absolute-mean benchmark and evidence is not a subgroup artifact; require coherence or validation. Benchmarks approximate: outcome_014 0.0093, outcome_001 0.0415, outcome_008 0.0282, outcome_011 0.0301, outcome_013 0.0269, outcome_006 0.0175. All findings are dataset-specific associations; no causality or generalizability inferred."
